<section id="wait"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="num rise">01 — THE WAIT</div>
  <div class="narrow rise">
    <div class="eyebrow">A Sunday, 7:30pm</div>
    <h2>The wait between asking and knowing</h2>
    <p class="lede">Three siblings in three cities are trying to work out whether their mother can afford this, whether she would be happy, and whether she would have to move again later. The pack answers all of it, somewhere, in eighty pages. Nobody reads eighty pages on a Sunday.</p>
    <p class="kicker" style="color:var(--accent)">Every retirement group in the country already publishes the material a worried family needs. The gap is never the information. It is that the information arrives in the order the brochure was written in, not the order this family is worried in.</p>
  </div>
  
  <!-- The wait itself, not three paragraphs about it. Same component the
       assembl homepage runs; see wait-phone.js. -->
  <div class="waitgrid rise">
    <div class="waitdemo">
      <div class="wp-invite">Live — the wait itself, not a picture of it. It stops to ask you one thing.</div>
      <div id="wait-mount"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="waitcards">
      <div class="glass" id="wait-explain"></div>
      <div class="glass tight"><h3 style="font-size:18px">What happens now</h3><p class="kicker" style="margin-top:10px;font-size:14px">One pack for every family. The questions it did not answer arrive by phone, one at a time, to whoever picks up.</p></div>
      <div class="glass tight"><h3 style="font-size:18px">What it costs</h3><p class="kicker" style="margin-top:10px;font-size:14px">The most emotionally loaded decision a family makes, handled with a document that does not know their situation.</p></div>
      <div class="glass tight"><h3 style="font-size:18px">What the concept does</h3><p class="kicker" style="margin-top:10px;font-size:14px">Opens the pack at the page that answers their worry, in their numbers, and stops. An advisor sends it.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  
  <div class="narrow rise" style="margin-top:64px">
    <div class="eyebrow">The principles it runs on</div>
    <h2 style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,30px)">Four rules, every moment.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="powgrid rise">
    <div class="pow"><i>01 — intent signal</i><b>The agent detects the wait</b><span>What the customer is waiting for, and why it matters right now.</span></div>
    <div class="pow"><i>02 — honest duration</i><b>How long, truthfully</b><span>Real steps, real progress. No fake bars, and never a wait stretched to fill.</span></div>
    <div class="pow"><i>03 — value delivery</i><b>Real work, done while they watch</b><span>The actual thing drafted and checked in front of the person, not a bar that fills.</span></div>
    <div class="pow"><i>04 — value exchange</i><b>The wait gives something back</b><span>Something real and theirs to keep, funded by the business, never by selling the person. One question comes back the other way.</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="prinline rise"><em>Opt-in, skippable, honest.</em> The reward comes from the business running the journey, never from selling the person waiting. Every decision still ends with a person.</p>

  <div class="narrow rise" style="margin-top:64px">
    <div class="eyebrow">Not one wait — a family of them</div>
    <h2 style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,30px)">Every village moment, one pattern.</h2>
    <p class="kicker">Each of these is a moment your customer already spends with you. Each can carry what the phone above shows: watch the work, earn the wait, answer one thing.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="momgrid rise">
    <div class="mom"><b>The enquiry</b><span>a pack, not a brochure</span></div>
    <div class="mom"><b>The visit</b><span>booked around the family</span></div>
